    "display_name": "Simulating a New Business",
    "long_instructions": "**Many new businesses wonder how fast they can grow.** \r\n\r\nWill they reach 1,000 customers, 10,000, or even 100,000? This kind of growth often happens through word of mouth. Happy customers tell their friends about a product, and those friends become customers too. This process can help a business grow quickly, much like a social media post going viral.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Update `simulate` so that it simulates how many months it will take a business to reach a target number of customers.\r\n- Ensure that, for each month, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Month {month}: {customers} customers\"`.\r\n- Choose and experiment with different arguments to `simulate`. Pay attention to how they change your simulation’s outcome.\r\n\r\n**🖥️ Coding Tip:**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python’s `while` loop can repeat code while a condition is true. For example:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ni = 1\r\nwhile i < 5:\r\n    print(i)\r\n    i += 1\r\n```",
